Hi Malcolm
I think you got needlessly tangled up here. Do not put your data in the package extdata folder. The example in secr-datainput.pdf <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-datainput.pdf> goes there just to retrieve some demo data that is distributed with the package. The only tricky thing is that for csv and text files secr requires that you explicitly to skip the header line (as in the xlsx example in that document). In this instance the error message is not useful, but that's R for you.
Murray

Try this:

library(secr)
setwd('d:/density users/malcolm soh')   # or your data folder
h23hr <- read.capthist(captfile = "H23hrcapt.csv", trapfile = "H23hrpoly.csv",
    fmt = "XY", detector = "polygon", skip = 1)
# No errors found :-)
plot(h23hr, tracks = TRUE)
summary(h23hr)
# Object class       capthist
# Detector type      polygon
# Number vertices    7
# Number polygons    1
# Total area         4.322366 ha
